# H2a (SOFT, quad, RUN LAST): the HANG PASS of H2, the four-card sub-device collective probe (scripts/ci/tp4_subdev_probe.py -> optimisation/ttnn-op/subdev_h/subdev_h2.py), under TT_METAL_WATCHER=5 AND
# TT_METAL_WATCHER_DISABLE_ETH=1 (both set by the probe). The first card run of this job (2026-10-10) died in open_mesh_device, before the first sub-device existed: with the watcher compiled into the fabric
# router's ethernet kernel its program is 28,256 bytes and the ACTIVE_ETH kernel config buffer is a fixed 25,600 (a constant of the HAL, whatever sub-device manager is loaded; Device::configure_fabric ->
# ProgramImpl::finalize_offsets). The ethernet switch compiles the watcher out of ethernet kernels only; the worker cores, where the gathers' workers and muxes run, stay watched.
# The fabric action opens the served (1, 4) ring once, with TWO command queues, creates the 80/30 sub-device manager, gives each sub-device its OWN double-buffered all-gather and barrier semaphores (created
# on its own cores), and runs the arms that CANNOT hang: a gather alone on each sub-device (eager, then traces of 24 gathers), then the two traces chained by an event, then both on one queue. Every gathered
# tensor is compared on every chip against the host's concatenation, after the output was overwritten with NaN. Untimed (the watcher distorts every wall).
# READ: 'SUBDEV_H2 verdict=UNTIMED-PASS' with watcher_errors=0; the watcher log is copied beside the report (subdev-watcher.log). STOP on FAIL-BYTES, a hang or any watcher error: H2b is skipped, Z resets.
# A per-call watchdog (exit 3), a heartbeat line every 30 s ('SUBDEV_H2 alive stage=...') and the box below are the stall watch.
# Needs the four cards, NO agentstop and NO agentstart here. Duration (estimate): 30 min (the box and the fabric step's own limit are below).
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the sub-device overlap programme (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of
# the window branch (a branch that carries optimisation/ttnn-op/subdev_h and scripts/ci/tp4_subdev_probe.py) and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the read rules and the minutes.
# C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next2-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag of the window's own image (sed -i 's/tp4-next2-1/<tag>/' *.env): this pack builds nothing, and any C2 image carries the tt-metal sub-device bindings
# it needs (the harnesses mount this checkout's files). The cards are under development: nothing here stops, starts or hands back the node agent.

C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset fabric
C2_FABRIC_PROBE=subdev-watch
C2_FABRIC=FABRIC_1D
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next2-1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=40
